I tried to only add animation where it actually meant something instead of just adding it for the sake of it. 
Like the radar sweep and the pulsing red dots in the hero — that's literally showing "we're monitoring right now,
" so it's not just decoration, it's part of the story. For hover effects on buttons and cards I kept the timing short
(like 0.2-0.3s) kyunke agar it's slower it starts feeling laggy instead of smooth. I didn't put any animation on the
CTA section or footer on purpose — after the hero and the scroll reveal already happened, adding more movement there
felt like too much, so I left it calm. Also for the scroll reveal I made it only trigger once per card, because when 
I was testing it, scrolling up and down and seeing the same fade-in play again and again got annoying real fast.
